WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
In episode twelve, I asked Sam to merge
orange day titles into the meal planner.

2
00:00:05.177 --> 00:00:07.927
Sam hasn't yet, and has been busy too.

3
00:00:08.026 --> 00:00:11.646
This time: what happens when two
people change the same thing.

4
00:00:11.853 --> 00:00:16.303
Here's what Sam did meanwhile: roomier
writing lines on the Day pages,

5
00:00:16.303 --> 00:00:19.223
saved and then published as a new version.

6
00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:21.377
I'll reload my request's page.

7
00:00:21.594 --> 00:00:23.324
It says conflicted now.

8
00:00:23.405 --> 00:00:25.745
Sam's save didn't change my request.

9
00:00:25.795 --> 00:00:29.673
A request is checked when it's
made, every time its page opens,

10
00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:31.954
and when the owner presses Merge.

11
00:00:32.012 --> 00:00:35.582
So one that was fine last
week can be conflicted today.

12
00:00:35.788 --> 00:00:39.101
The line under the title says
it can't be merged as-is.

13
00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:42.448
The red Conflicts box says
why: the Day template,

14
00:00:42.448 --> 00:00:45.974
in the default variant,
was changed on both sides.

15
00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.976
We didn't touch the same thing on
the page: I colored the title,

16
00:00:49.976 --> 00:00:51.710
Sam spaced out the lines.

17
00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:54.671
But changes are compared a
whole template at a time,

18
00:00:54.671 --> 00:00:57.743
so two different edits to
the Day template collide.

19
00:00:57.888 --> 00:01:00.108
An edit to the Week page wouldn't have.

20
00:01:00.313 --> 00:01:05.512
The page hierarchy is a single unit too,
including what's typed into the pages.

21
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:09.037
If we'd both added a page,
that would collide as well.

22
00:01:09.246 --> 00:01:10.896
Here's why it can't merge.

23
00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.333
Merging doesn't copy my
fork over Sam's project.

24
00:01:14.379 --> 00:01:17.887
It takes what I changed since
forking, the Day template,

25
00:01:17.887 --> 00:01:20.519
and lays it over Sam's latest version.

26
00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:22.779
That would quietly undo the new lines.

27
00:01:22.984 --> 00:01:25.184
So nothing is merged by guesswork.

28
00:01:25.276 --> 00:01:30.198
A conflicted request has no Merge
button, not even for Sam, only Close.

29
00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:33.079
And the server checks
again before any merge.

30
00:01:33.284 --> 00:01:35.864
There's no button that fixes a conflict.

31
00:01:35.976 --> 00:01:40.735
As the page says, I fork the latest
version and propose my changes again:

32
00:01:40.735 --> 00:01:42.876
that's the fork author's job.

33
00:01:43.022 --> 00:01:47.072
First, I'll close this request:
it can't be merged as it stands.

34
00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:50.349
Then I fork Sam's planner again.

35
00:01:50.463 --> 00:01:54.333
Fork copies the published version,
so the new lines come with it.

36
00:01:54.453 --> 00:01:59.365
Had Sam only saved them, a new request
would be conflicted the moment I made it.

37
00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.680
In Templates, the Day template
already has Sam's roomier lines.

38
00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:07.979
Now I make my change again, on
top of Sam's: the title, orange.

39
00:02:10.743 --> 00:02:15.326
Save to cloud first, because a request
always proposes the latest save,

40
00:02:15.326 --> 00:02:17.513
never what's only in this tab.

41
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.880
Then Propose changes to upstream.

42
00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:23.911
The note tells Sam it's the same
change, redone on top of Sam's.

43
00:02:28.943 --> 00:02:33.418
The new request is open: the same
single change, and no conflicts.

44
00:02:33.456 --> 00:02:39.086
Render before and after shows Sam's current
page, then the same page with my title.

45
00:02:39.293 --> 00:02:43.883
When Sam merges, my change set is
laid over Sam's latest version.

46
00:02:43.986 --> 00:02:48.694
I made it on top of that, so both
survive: roomy lines, orange titles.

47
00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.971
Sam merges it from the other side.

48
00:02:51.114 --> 00:02:53.794
One reload, and my request says merged.

49
00:02:56.427 --> 00:03:01.093
So: requests are checked every time they
open, conflicts are never merged by

50
00:03:01.093 --> 00:03:05.027
guesswork, and the fork author
fixes them with a fresh fork.

51
00:03:05.166 --> 00:03:08.154
Next time: reaching elements
buried under others.
